{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-13_20-21-32-hashicorp_raft-real-run && python3 - <<'PYEOF'\nimport json\np='draft/update.json'\nd=json.load(open(p))\nd['rationale']=(\\\"The extended probe now also reaches two-sided acknowledgement: polling for the majority side's own leader before writing lets both leaders commit and acknowledge a client write while partitioned, so the run shows a client write acknowledged on each side (both_sides_acknowledged true on the flagged case, false for the flag-off control where only the majority side acknowledges). FSM divergence and lost acknowledged entries are still not witnessed, because the applied-slice indexing did not line up with the conflict index and the heal window is short; that part is left open. This successor declares the two-sided acknowledgement as a bounded check for a receipt; the configuration, election and single-side acknowledgement comparisons remain as recorded.\\\")\ne=dict(d['experiment']) if d.get('experiment') else {}\ne.pop('previous_id',None)\ne['investigation_id']=\\\"9eb7105d2f8e48dfa54fcc262ad69cd9-question-0\\\"\nd['experiment']={\n \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"9eb7105d2f8e48dfa54fcc262ad69cd9-question-0\\\",\n \\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"assurance_generated_test.go\\\",\n \\\"previous_id\\\":\\\"758774f1aea1458fb581c68df9d6ce88-experiment\\\",\n \\\"revision_reason\\\":\\\"The probe now waits (bounded to three seconds) for the majority side to have its own leader before writing, so both sides can acknowledge concurrently, and the event carries a derived both_sides_acknowledged operand so the comparison is inspectable. Scenario, isolation, apply and heal steps are unchanged.\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"api_restore_committed_body\\\",\\\"api_addvoter\\\",\\\"api_apply_contract\\\",\\\"raft_quorum_size\\\",\\\"raft_electself_vote_count\\\"],\n \\\"scope\\\":{\\\"description\\\":\\\"Five-voter cluster whose leading node is restarted with RestoreCommittedLogs after a snapshot predating the membership change, isolated with one committed voter immediately after the restart. Once the isolated node is leader and the majority side has its own leader, a client Apply is issued on both; the partition is healed, and the event reports whether both sides acknowledged. Run with the flag on and off.\\\",\n  \\\"assumptions\\\":[\\\"The isolated node's rebuilt configuration is the three-voter snapshot configuration, so two votes commit there while the committed configuration needs three.\\\",\\\"A successful Apply is an acknowledgement to the client.\\\",\\\"Waiting for both sides to hold leadership is a legal partition shape, not an injected fault.\\\"],\n  \\\"excluded\\\":[\\\"Whole-package or repository test suites.\\\",\\\"FSM divergence and lost-entry claims; the applied-slice comparison at the conflict index did not line up and is not used.\\\",\\\"Entry contents at the conflict index, which the probe reports as empty.\\\"],\n  \\\"parameters\\\":{\\\"voters_before\\\":3,\\\"voters_after\\\":5,\\\"isolation\\\":\\\"immediately after restart\\\",\\\"majority_leader_wait_seconds\\\":3,\\\"apply_timeout_seconds\\\":2,\\\"heal_settle_seconds\\\":2}},\n \\\"prefix\\\":\\\"The harness reuses the multi-voter scenario construction (MakeClusterCustom with Peers 3, CommitTrackingLogs and RestoreCommittedLogs; one deliberate Snapshot; MakeClusterNoBootstrap(2) merged with FullyConnect and two AddVoter calls; Shutdown and NewRaft on the same stores with a fresh inmem transport; Partition isolating the restarted node plus one committed voter with that pair reconnected). It waits for the isolated node to be leader, waits up to three seconds for a majority-side leader, applies a distinct command on each side, heals by reconnecting all transports, waits two seconds, and emits mvdiv_after_heal with both leaders' presence, both apply outcomes, the derived both_sides_acknowledged operand, the conflict index, the applied slice lengths and the FSM divergence flag; no production logic is modified.\\\",\n \\\"responsibility\\\":\\\"The library owns the acknowledgement it gives a client and the guarantee that a committed entry survives; with a stale rebuilt configuration both depend on a quorum of an obsolete membership.\\\",\n \\\"prerequisites\\\":[\n  {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"div_on\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"startup_before_restart\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"div_on\\\"},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"snapshots\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":1},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"expected_servers\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":5}]},\n  {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"div_off\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"startup_before_restart\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"div_off\\\"},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"snapshots\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":1},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"expected_servers\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":5}]}],\n \\\"comparisons\\\":[\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"mvdiv_after_heal\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"mode\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"div_on\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"both_sides_acknowledged\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},\n   \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"restore_committed_logs\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"snapshots\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":1}],\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"Two partitioned sides must not both acknowledge client writes while one of them holds only a minority of the committed configuration; the defect prediction is that both do.\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"mvdiv_after_heal\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"mode\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"div_off\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"both_sides_acknowledged\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},\n   \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"restore_committed_logs\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"snapshots\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":1}],\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"Control: with the committed configuration rebuilt the isolated side has no leader, so only the majority side acknowledges.\\\"}]}\nit=d['interpretations'][0]\nit['rationale']=it['rationale'].replace(\\\"Not witnessed: any FSM divergence or lost acknowledged entry, because no run produced a majority-side leader that wrote concurrently.\\\",\\\"A fourth check is under test: with a bounded wait for a majority-side leader before writing, a native run had both sides acknowledge a client write concurrently (both_sides_acknowledged true on the flagged case, false for the control, where only the majority side acknowledges), which the successor experiment re-runs for a receipt. Not witnessed: any FSM divergence or lost acknowledged entry, because the applied-slice comparison at the conflict index did not line up and no entry was recovered after healing.\\\")\njson.dump(d,open(p,'w'),indent=2)\nprint('ok')\nPYEOF\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-13_20-21-32-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -3\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
